-1-3.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c21-t1-l-g3-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 21-22","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">21</strong><strong class=\"source-question-number\">22</strong><span>Which TWO features of the lecture on ocean biodiversity had the greatest impact on the students?</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>the references to local problems</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>the broad focus of the examples</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>the practical suggestions for solutions</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">D</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"D\"></span><span>the type of issues discussed</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">E</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"E\"></span><span>the implications for government policy</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":1},{"id":"en-c21-t1-l-g3-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 23-24","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">23</strong><strong class=\"source-question-number\">24</strong><span>Which TWO details about the research project particularly impressed the students?</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>the team's previous successes</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>its wide geographical scale</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>the use of new technology</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">D</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"D\"></span><span>the extensive statistical evidence</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">E</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"E\"></span><span>the large range of specialists involved</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":1},{"id":"en-c21-t1-l-g3-2","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 25-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>What is the students' opinion of each of the following resources related to ocean biodiversity?</p><p>Choose SIX answers from the box and write the correct letter, A-H, next to Questions 25-30.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"matching-dnd-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Article on invasive lionfish<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Documentary on microplastics<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Podcast on ocean pollution<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Book on coastal ecosystems<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Article on metal toxicity<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Podcast on floating marine cities<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--matching\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This is aimed at a very specialist audience.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This is now rather outdated.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This was an effective description of a new danger.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This suggests possible ways to improve the situation.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"E\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">E.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This does not give a balanced account.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"F\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">F.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This is too predictable to be useful.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"G\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">G.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This gives insufficient evidence for its claims.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"H\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">H.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">This gives a clear explanation of the problems.</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":6}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-21-academic-listening-test-1-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c21-t1-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3178719-cambridge-ielts-21-academic-listening-test-1-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c21-t1-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.</p><p><strong>Sources of rubber</strong></p><p>Three resources which are essential for industrial civilisation</p><ul><li><span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>fossil fuels</li><li>rubber</li></ul><p><strong>Natural rubber</strong></p><p>This mainly comes from the Pará rubber tree, now cultivated in South-East Asia. The supply is limited because</p><ul><li>the growth of the tree is <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li><li>production cannot easily be adjusted because of increasing or decreasing <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li><li>the tree only grows near the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li><li>extracting the latex (rubber) is labour-intensive</li><li>it is very difficult to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> rubber after production.</li></ul><p><strong>New threats include</strong></p><ul><li>lack of genetic diversity, leading to danger of disease caused by a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li><li>a shift to the cultivation of palm oil</li><li>extreme <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> events.</li></ul><p><strong>Synthetic rubber</strong></p><ul><li>may be used for engine parts and cooking utensils</li><li>is less <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> than natural rubber</li><li>is unsuitable for many purposes e.g. the tyres of aircraft.</li></ul><p><strong>An alternative source of natural rubber</strong></p><ul><li>A wild flower (a type of dandelion) has rubber in its <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li><li>It can be grown in many locations and does not require good <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c21-t1-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-21-academic-listening-test-1-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c21-t1-l-q1","part_id":"en-c21-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c21-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"10/ten","correct_answer_variants":["10","ten"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3178393_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c21-t1-l-q2","part_id":"en-c21-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c21-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"weather","correct_answer_variants":["weather"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3178393_2","order_ind